  r115b_ohm: {value: 100000.0, source: 'sch: R115B printed 180K LIN on this scan; web: https://groupdiy.com/threads/whats-this-symbol-in-the-fairchild-670-diagram.35361/ (Walrus: the original manual shows ''a dual 100k lin tapped pot''; CJ: ''the 100k looks like 180k on some prints''). Nominal 100K: two readers of other prints, and matched sections give both 12AX7 grids the same drive (180K with a 50% tap gives that grid 3 dB less below the tap)', genome: sidechain_threshold.r115b_ohm}
